WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.912
Small studios still copy paper sewing patterns by hand, or pay for a digitizing table.

00:00:06.733 --> 00:00:15.641
easyon-scan needs one phone photo with printed marker cards around the pattern, and returns a closed DXF outline in millimetres.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:19.893
New: lens calibration and photo quality checks.

00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:24.486
A distorted or blurry photo is rejected, not silently measured.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.924
Several pieces with holes in one photo, plus notches and grain lines.

00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:36.245
An experimental AAMA and ASTM style export.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:41.560
Guided capture checks markers, sharpness and tilt before you shoot.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:45.606
And large patterns can be joined from several photos.

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:49.946
Every number here comes from synthetic photos.

00:00:49.946 --> 00:00:53.382
Accuracy on real photos is not validated yet.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.552
Try it in five minutes.

00:00:55.552 --> 00:00:56.551
It's open source.

